\begin{align*}
\frac{ab + bc + cd}{3} &\geq \sqrt[3]{ab \cdot bc \cdot cd} \\
\frac{ab + bc + cd}{3} &\geq \sqrt[3]{a^2b^2c^2d^2} \\
\end{align*}
Since $a + b + c + d = 1$, by AM-GM inequality, we have:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{4}(a + b + c + d) &\geq \sqrt[4]{abcd} \\
\frac{1}{4} &\geq \sqrt[4]{abcd} \\
\end{align*}
Squaring both sides, we get:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{16} &\geq abcd \\
\end{align*}
Multiplying both sides by 3 and taking the square root of both sides, we have:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\frac{3}{16}} &\geq \sqrt[3]{a^2b^2c^2d^2} \\
\end{align*}
Substituting this into our inequality, we get:
\begin{align*}
\frac{ab + bc + cd}{3} &\geq \sqrt[3]{a^2b^2c^2d^2} \\
ab + bc + cd &\geq 3\sqrt[3]{a^2b^2c^2d^2} \\
&\geq 3\sqrt[3]{\frac{3}{16}} \\
&= \frac{3\sqrt{3}}{4} \\
